Description: enable V-Sync, handle window close and fix command line flags
 * Call SDL_GL_SetSwapInterval(1) right after SDL_GL_CreateContext, so that
   the intro is synchronised with the display instead of rendering as fast
   as possible.
 * Read the real drawable size after the window creation, so that the
   viewport is right when the intro starts in fullscreen.
 * Use desktop fullscreen for -f (no video mode change).
 * -n/--no-fullscreen toggled the fullscreen flag, so it switched to
   fullscreen when the default is windowed: it is now the same as -w.
 * Process all pending events each frame, quit on SDL_QUIT (window close
   button), and ignore key repeat of F.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-14
